{"metadata":{"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","text":"RefreshAction"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","title":"refresh","roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI17EnvironmentValuesV7refreshAA13RefreshActionVSgvp"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When this environment value contains an instance of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" structure, certain built-in views in the corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" begin offering a refresh capability. They apply the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance’s handler to any refresh operation that the user initiates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By default, the environment value is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but you can use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"View\/refreshable(action:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier to create and store a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refresh action that uses the handler that you specify:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["List(mailbox.conversations) { conversation in","    ConversationCell(conversation)","}",".refreshable {","    await mailbox.fetch()","}"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS and iPadOS, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"List","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the example above offers a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pull to refresh gesture because it detects the refresh action. When","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user drags the list down and releases, the list calls the action’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler. Because SwiftUI declares the handler as asynchronous, it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"safely make long-running asynchronous calls, like fetching network data.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Refreshing Custom Views","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Refreshing-Custom-Views"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also offer refresh capability in your custom views.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Read the ","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" environment value to get the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance for a given ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". If you find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a non-","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, change your view’s appearance or behavior to offer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the refresh to the user, and call the instance to conduct the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refresh. You can call the refresh instance directly because it defines","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method that Swift calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when you call the instance:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct RefreshableView: View {","    @Environment(\\.refresh) private var refresh","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Refresh\") {","            Task {","                await refresh?()","            }","        }","        .disabled(refresh == nil)","    }","}"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Be sure to call the handler asynchronously by preceding it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":". Because the call is asynchronous, you can use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its lifetime to indicate progress to the user. For example,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can reveal an indeterminate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProgressView"},{"text":" before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calling the handler, and hide it when the handler completes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your code isn’t already in an asynchronous context, create a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/Task","type":"text"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method to run in. If you do this, consider adding a way for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user to cancel the task. For more information, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Programming Language"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"OpenSwiftUI exposes a collection of values to your app’s views in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"EnvironmentValues","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structure. To read a value from the structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declare a property using the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" property wrapper and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specify the value’s key path. For example, you can read the current locale:","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"